<title>HONG KONG: Advance unit of China PLA troops enters Hong Kong.</title>
<headline>Advance unit of China PLA troops enters Hong Kong.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>An advance unit of China's People's Liberation Army (PLA) took an historic step into Hong Kong on Monday when they arrived to prepare garrison facilities for China's July 1 takeover of the territory from Britain.  </p>
<p>The 40-strong advance unit drove into the British colony in PLA staff cars at the Lok Ma Chau land crossing at 1 pm (0500 GMT).</p>
<p>They are due to head for the Prince of Wales Barracks of the British armed forces in downtown Hong Kong.</p>
</text>
